# ls-foundry — no manual package publish

Agents must **not** publish npm packages from the local machine.

## Do not run (unless the user explicitly asks)

- `npm publish` / `pnpm publish`
- `pnpm run deploy` / `pnpm run deploy:changed`
- `scripts/publish-changed.sh`
- Any other command that uploads `@jeffgo10/*` to GitHub Packages

## Why

1. Changes are often still **uncommitted** when work finishes; a local publish races ahead of git.
2. Push/merge to **`master`** already triggers `.github/workflows/publish-packages.yml` → `scripts/publish-changed.sh`.
3. Publishing locally then merging the same version bump can **conflict**, confuse consumers, or force awkward republish work.

## What agents should do instead

1. **Bump** `packages/*/package.json` versions (and pin tables) when changing `@jeffgo10/*` — see `ls-foundry-core.mdc`.
2. Build/test locally as needed (`pnpm run build:packages`, `pnpm test`).
3. Commit / open a PR only when the user asks (`/create-github-pr`).
4. After merge, CI publishes. Confirm with `npm view` **only if the user asks**, and only after the version exists on `master`.

## Exception

Run publish/deploy **only** when the user explicitly requests it in the current message (e.g. “publish now”, “run deploy”). Do not infer publish from “done”, “ship it”, or a prior task checklist.
